WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.898
Stage four: talk to your coach.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.862
Camille feels drained. In the Coach tab, one sentence is enough.

3
00:00:09.962 --> 00:00:12.324
Should the threshold still happen?

4
00:00:13.174 --> 00:00:18.728
The coach answers in the open: every file read, every tool called, shown.

5
00:00:18.828 --> 00:00:24.910
H R V thirty-eight, resting heart rate fifty-two, readiness thirty-four.

6
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:32.946
It suggests easing off: forty-five easy minutes. But nothing reaches Garmin without your approval.

7
00:00:33.046 --> 00:00:37.616
Camille clicks Apply: session scheduled, decision written.

8
00:00:38.466 --> 00:00:43.084
And Saturday? The coach keeps the long run, with an early start.

9
00:00:44.466 --> 00:00:49.204
The coach reads the workspace and Garmin, and writes your Markdown files.

10
00:00:49.304 --> 00:00:56.322
But any write to Garmin or Intervals.icu waits for your approval. A free shell? Refused.

11
00:00:57.172 --> 00:01:03.398
The chat stays local: the dashboard listens on 127.0.0.1.

12
00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:08.092
And spending is capped: one euro per turn, two per day.

13
00:01:08.942 --> 00:01:12.432
On a phone, the card stays front and centre.

14
00:01:12.532 --> 00:01:17.942
Unanswered, a notification summarises the change, with no health data.

15
00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:24.850
An API key, not your subscription: Claude, or OpenRouter with DeepSeek.

16
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:29.712
Here, replies are scripted: a demo backend, no cost.

17
00:01:32.262 --> 00:01:36.496
To go further: the “Chat with the coach” page of the documentation.
